      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`Hf3fsUsrBioClient.batch_write` copied every page into the shm staging buffer, prepared all I/Os, and only then submitted once. So no write I/O could start until every page had been copied and prepared.\n\nThe write path also had two correctness issues:\n- Results were read in prepare order, but 3FS returns completions in completion order.\n- On a `wait()` timeout or error, the call returned with I/O still in flight. The next call could then overwrite a shm region or ring slot that was still in use.\n\n## Modifications\n\nAll changes are in `hf3fs_usrbio_client.py`:\n- `batch_write` now copies, prepares and submits each page in turn, so a page's I/O starts before the next page is copied. `check()` limits a batch to `entries` pages, so each page has its own ring slot and shm region.\n- New `_wait_all`: maps results by `userdata` (the page index), and waits out every prepared I/O, through partial waits, `wait()` errors and past `client_timeout`, before returning.\n\n`batch_read` is unchanged.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\n**Setup:** standalone client benchmark (`bench_client.py`, not part of this PR) on a 3FS cluster. File size 2 GiB, 16 MiB pages, `numjobs=1`, `entries=8`, 3 warmup + 10 timed iterations. Baseline is this PR's parent commit. Base and PR runs were interleaved, 8 repeats each.\n\n| | WRITE p50 (GiB/s), median of 8 | vs base |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| base | 2.92 | — |\n| this PR | 5.33 | **1.82×** |\n\n- This PR beat base in 8 of 8 paired repeats, by 1.39× to 2.41×.\n- A single-run sweep over page size (1–16 MiB) × `entries` (2–32) found no slowdown beyond noise. 1–4 MiB pages still gained 1.2–2.1×.\n- READ is unchanged.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39194718060](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39194718060)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39194717942](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39194717942)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39194718038](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39194718038)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
